    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f172d2f3_4b05c822",
        "filename": "startop/tools/view_compiler/dex_builder.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 55,
      "author": {
        "id": 1335232
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-15T18:54:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Eventually this is going to have a static method that creates new type descriptors from a class name [1]. The idea I\u0027m going for is that you can do TypeDescriptor::INT, TypeDescriptor::VOID, TypeDescriptor::FromClass(\"classname\"), etc. I\u0027d like to keep all of the \"constructors\" in the same named scope, and TypeDescriptor seems as good as creating a new Type namespace to me.\n\n[1]: http://aosp/c/platform/frameworks/base/+/787818/1/startop/view_compiler/dex_builder.h#60",
      "parentUuid": "2f9969cf_ff67c436",
      "revId": "bd5bebfe30867d79fa6e415739bbf4e9b24d4c2d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8dc5b70e_3eec537d",
        "filename": "startop/tools/view_compiler/dex_builder.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 55,
      "author": {
        "id": 1047255
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-15T22:07:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My preference would still be to put these in a separate namespace, as I think it would make the code easier to read.  That is just my opinion though, and the code is more than fine the way it is.",
      "parentUuid": "f172d2f3_4b05c822",
      "revId": "bd5bebfe30867d79fa6e415739bbf4e9b24d4c2d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "74769e6b_c63bcb22",
        "filename": "startop/tools/view_compiler/dex_builder.h",
