      "writtenOn": "2018-10-11T21:42:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This can be conflated with the object-oriented notion of Prototype.  Is it consistent with other Dex terminology?  Could it be re-named to FunctionSignature?",
      "revId": "bd5bebfe30867d79fa6e415739bbf4e9b24d4c2d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01bdc665_1a31589d",
        "filename": "startop/tools/view_compiler/dex_builder.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 71,
      "author": {
        "id": 1335232
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-15T18:54:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The existing code and documentation all works with proto or prototype. For example: https://source.android.com/devices/tech/dalvik/dex-format#proto-id-item\n\nI personally like Signature better, but here I think Prototype is better due to its consistency with existing usage. Since C++ and the Java Language are not prototype OO languages, I don\u0027t think the confusion is as big of a concern here.",
      "parentUuid": "0ea3507e_4ba959b7",
      "revId": "bd5bebfe30867d79fa6e415739bbf4e9b24d4c2d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
